{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th","id":1530740,"title":"Hypothetical - If we were to update WTA to 5th Edition using 20th...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-02-13T07:02:01-08:00","id":1530740,"title":"Hypothetical - If we were to update WTA to 5th Edition using 20th...","content":"ICONS OF RAGE is awesome and OPP is the last gasp of the heavy continuity of the previous editions that we all fell in love with. So, the question would be how would you update the setting to the year 2024?<br /> <br /> Assuming that Gaia isn't dead or dying and the Cult of Fenris didn't exist.<br /> <br /> Feel free to suggest big changes but we're using W20 as a basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T08:20:07-08:00","id":1530744,"title":"","content":"From what I understand wolf populations are a actually pretty good ATM so it could be interesting to run a lupus resurface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T15:13:53-08:00","id":1530763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1530744#post1530744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I understand wolf populations are a actually pretty good ATM so it could be interesting to run a lupus resurface.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the massacre of them in a certain state by state law seems like it would be a possible interesting Chronicle in itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-13T17:34:54-08:00","id":1530770,"title":"","content":"This was definitely a harder question than I expected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T01:43:06-08:00","id":1530793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1530763#post1530763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the massacre of them in a certain state by state law seems like it would be a possible interesting Chronicle in itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually reverse it, the whole concept of the lupus and the Red Talons has been that they are a dying breed. If that no longer is the case and if there are suddenly MORE lupus than most modern garou are used to it would create a lot of political strife as the formerly very human-minded tribes have to readjust to the wolf-mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T06:02:57-08:00","id":1530805,"title":"","content":"I tend to agree - showing wolf (and Lupus) populations on the rise would be a good way to show Garou having a positive impact on the world, without actually making life easier for them - given that just about everything else in the World of Darkness knows that if you want a shot at the Garou, hitting the wolves who go on four legs is a good place to start.<br /> <br /> Also, seeing the Red Talon struggling to come to terms with the distinct possibility that humans have actually done wolves a solid for once would be something worth seeing (If only because this would potentially allow authors to back off a bit from making this tribe all Hauglosk, all the time).<br /> <br /> <br /> It actually might be interesting to borrow some ideas from 5th Edition and see what the classic editions make of them - for example the very notion that Hauglosk exists and is an actual problem would almost certainly trigger some fascinating controversies throughout the Garou Nation (Not least because there would be some serious potential for \u2018Well that explains a lot\u2019 moments).<br /> <br /> Seeing elements within the Glass Walkers advocate a shift from Cockroach to Spider would also be intriguing: if nothing else this would give us some interesting perspective on how a Tribe\u2019s relationship with their Patron Spirit shifts across time (and whether it\u2019s a Tribe that makes the Totem or the Totem that makes the Tribe).<br /> <br /> The Black Spiral Dancers having a rather more bloody variation of the same seismic shift might also be intriguing (Especially if it ends with Bat, a patron spirit partly restored to Gaia, at the top).<br /> <br /> <br /> In all honesty, though, I\u2019m not sure how contemporary WW20 ought to be: to my mind it\u2019s the \u2018timeless\u2019 version of the classic editions (Where on a good day it\u2019s six minutes to midnight and on a bad day it\u2019s never more than five), which need only touch upon current events if a Chronicle requires it to be.<br /> <br /> Oddly enough my gut instinct is that the By Night studios version of WEREWOLF might be the more interesting one to update to AD 2024, since as an effectively post-apocalyptic (or at least Post-Apocalypse War) setting there\u2019s more room to show significant changes having occurred.<br /> <br /> Now I just need to finish reading that sourcebook to make sure this isn\u2019t a mistaken impression!\ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-19T18:02:02-08:00","id":1531157,"title":"","content":"The biggest change I'd make is reworking tribes. All Fera should have them, they should line up vaguely with biogeographical regions or taxonomic boundaries (at least before factoring in immigration and population movement), and they should look more like an actual ethnic group than the special interest group/political parties that we got. There'd be more than thirteen; the thirteen tribes we know would simply be the biggest ones and you'd be given instructions on how to create your own tribes for a chronicle. Camps would take a similar role tribes do now and be cross-tribal by default. Some of the traditional aspects would still be present, but they'd be downplayed and largely due to the tribe forming alliances with specific spirits. The Glass Walkers aren't all city-dwellers or good with technology, they just formed an alliance with urban spirits and that influences their gift list. The Talons aren't uniting around hatred of the human species, it's just that their patron spirit only allows wolf and crinos-born and they spend a lot of time hanging around the spirits of extinct and endangered animals, which tends to color their opinions.<br /> <br /> This means that tribes can blend to some extent for Kinfolk; someone could be bitribal. Fera can't, at least not by how Fera figure it, because initiation involves rites to bind you to the patron spirit and those are exclusive. You can switch tribes or choose to join one that you aren't related to, but they won't necessarily take you and there tends to be <i>extremely</i> heavy pressure to assimilate if you do. This, and the lesser pressure placed on human and animal-born to assimilate, is a source of tension.<br /> <br /> I'd get rid of mythological patron spirits; I think patron spirits should be organisms or natural phenomena in the region a tribe comes from.<br /> <br /> Caerns would be emphasized as more than just a center of Fera culture. There'd be more rites that influenced a caern's bawn--potential choices might be ones to increase rainfall, shred the Gauntlet, reduce temperatures, or increase plant growth. Some of these could have minor regional effects, especially if done at a powerful caern. There would also be fetishes which would extend the range of a caern's effect or have permanent effects on the local bawn so long as they're fed gnosis regularly.<br /> <br /> I'd make it so that normal humans and animals could become Kinfolk by hanging around caerns long enough. It's not assured, but it'd common enough if they're spending a year or so on the bawn--the energies of the caern allow for the patrons of the Fera to transform them. This would be a retcon. In addition, simply due to the numbers disparity and the Curse, Fera have to lean more on their Kinfolk and their Kinfolk are treated more (though not completely) equally. A squad of Kinfolk with guns is a significant asset, and there are many Crafts of Kinfolk mages or sorcerers. Nonhuman Kinfolk would get more time devoted to them and show up more often as NPCs. They would be supported as PCs again (and yes, this <i>does </i>mean you can play a lupus Kinfolk mage). I would also leave the Fera-Kinfolk birth ratio undefined, because the math makes no sense, and change the focus of Fera population problems from &quot;They have a low birth rate&quot; to &quot;They die <i>a lot.&quot; </i>Fera births would still be uncommon, though. I think this would solve most of the problems people have with Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Crinos-born would get a new name, as would Younger and Older Brother. Bigotry towards crinos-born for being the result of a violation of the Litany would get toned down, but still be present.<br /> <br /> In terms of metaplot, the Fera continue to lose the war but have started working out more of their internal issues--continuing the trend from Revised. The Ahadi are now a solid alliance that clearly isn't going anywhere. I don't really have metaplot ideas for other stuff, but since I'm interested in Werewolf/Mage crossover I would probably have the Technocracy starting to show up as an antagonist.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1530805#post1530805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, seeing the Red Talon struggling to come to terms with the distinct possibility that humans have actually done wolves a solid for once would be something worth seeing (If only because this would potentially allow authors to back off a bit from making this tribe all Hauglosk, all the time).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Talons aren't going to see it that way. While the death-cult that is the Predator Kings will decrease in prominence, the Talons aren't going to give humans credit for translocating a few packs, easing up <i>just</i> enough to make sure they don't outright go extinct, and then generally killing 30% of their population every year--especially when the whole mess was caused by humans in the first place. What probably happens is that both the Predator Kings and the Whelp's Compromise shrink.<br /> <br /> I do think the Talons could have a major role in improving relations with other Fera, or at least animal-born Fera. Part of what I'd do if I was creating a new edition would be to make the animal-born, across species, start to see themselves as more of a cohesive group with unifying interests. The Talons would be obvious choices for Garou to get involved in those politics, especially since their African offshoots helped found the Ahadi. From a game design role, having the Talons be more politically progressive in some ways makes the times when PCs <i>do</i> clash with them more compelling and also makes them more appealing as player characters or PC allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-22T15:49:23-08:00","id":1531314,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar28383_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"28383\" data-vbnamecard=\"28383\">Citrakayah</a>, I don\u2019t agree with all your notions (I\u2019m especially against losing the Mythological Patron Spirits, as a way of keeping the Garou\u2019s essential nature as Heroes out of an Age of Myth struggling to hold on in the Modern Age), but I do think that a great many of them have merit.<br /> <br /> My congratulations on expressing your ideas with such clarity and conviction.\ud83d\ude04","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-01T13:23:28-08:00","id":1531800,"title":"","content":"I generally don't like the implication of Hauglusk. The Garou are not responsible for the horrors they did because they couldn't help themselves. They were built shoddily and thanks to that they will only end their life in depression or destructive madness. You are a monster not because of the choices you made, but because a switch flipped in your spirit/brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T10:12:46-08:00","id":1531846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1531800#post1531800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I generally don't like the implication of Hauglusk. The Garou are not responsible for the horrors they did because they couldn't help themselves. They were built shoddily and thanks to that they will only end their life in depression or destructive madness. You are a monster not because of the choices you made, but because a switch flipped in your spirit/brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also takes away nuance which was very important in the setting. The Litany had no one reading, different tribes vouched for different methods and so on. The point was that there was no one answer to the problem.<br /> <br /> Hauglosk is bad. Not only that but it exists outside the story, because so many example characters take actions that should incur it and yet they are not stated to have any. So Hauglosk for these characters starts existing ONLY when they enter the play, which makes no sense storywise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T12:14:28-08:00","id":1531849,"title":"","content":"The &quot;only in play&quot; reminds me of the conundrums I experience when thinking about BattleTech's Enhanced Imagining Implants with ProtoMech pilots. Having an EI implant causes the irreversible accrual of permanent fatigue points at a set rate. In order to even pilot a ProtoMech, you have to have an EI implant... but you also need many years of training after said implant is installed. Yet, starting characters with EI implants do not start with any permanent fatigue.<br /> <br /> At least BT has the excuse that some of the early years can potentially be obviated by the rehab period that the implant requires (an entire year just to get your nervous system working correctly again!) and the resistance of the Aerospace phenotype to its negative effects (one point every three years instead of one per year). There's no indication that there could be extenuating circumstances in W5 without buying a single example of an expensive loresheet and being an ex-CoF... somehow, or a rare fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T13:07:48-08:00","id":1531850,"title":"","content":"It also puts Red Talons and their example characters in a truly interesting light. Hauglosk is supposed to be about taking things too far and therefore breaking chronicle tenets. Yet, the Plague Dog exists and by all rights should end up in Hauglosk within 5 sessions if the ST isn't going for a 'humans are the real monsters' type of game.<br /> <br /> This creates a situation where some extremist behaviour is allowed no matter how harsh, but other such behaviour is not. Because we are given CoF as the strawman and poster tribe for Hauglosk and there is so far no non-CoF case of Hauglosk in canon, the message is not &quot;Don't go too far.&quot; It is &quot;Don't be a CoF.&quot;<br /> <br /> This completely ruins whatever message the mechanic could have had. Instead, it shows us a faction that exists only as a strawman for the PCs to put down rather than a nuanced example of how no one is immune to falling victim to extremism. Then we add the allowed actions per the character examples and you end up with VERY unfortunate writing.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-02T13:18:27-08:00","id":1531851,"title":"","content":"The problem with Hauglosk is also that as a narrative tool it doesn't quite work. With Harano at least, it's easy to figure out the narrative arc you're pursuing. Shit happens, defeats, losses, failures... it all piles up until the point where your character just gives up. Easy to see what this is going for in terms of a narrative. Although, I don't think the write-up of Harano in the W5 corebook is particularly good as it takes the lazy shortcut of just going for &quot;supernatural depression&quot; but that's a whole other issue.<br /> <br /> I mentioned in other threads how I would change Hauglosk and the first thing is that its definition needs to be fundamentally changed. Because as it's presented, the idea is that <i>every single Garou</i> is on track to potentially becoming a fanatical, self-righteous asshole. The only way this could work is if everybody at the table buys into the very negative portrayal of Garou you get in the W5 corebook. But Hauglosk is less a condition and more a description for a distinct characterization anyway. Even the way it's described shows that. It's about losing your way in how you fight the war. But that's a character-issue, something that applies to certain characters under specific circumstances. It isn't this state of being that every Garou is doomed to slip into.<br /> <br /> Even in the examples offered, like this one from pg 52 of the W5 corebook:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> An aging Silver Fang grows jealous of the achievements of younger Garou. The stories of his accomplishments fade; the enemies he fought, forgotten. Desperate to feel as if he still matters, he resorts to calling for the killing of everyone who\u2019s ever worked at a certain Pentex Group front in the territory, from board members to drug store clerks. He argues that, once the corporate evil took root, the community could not be redeemed. The pack has to decide whether they agree with the policy of mass extermination and, if not, how to stop it. Is it possible to talk the Silver Fang out of it? If not, how can they bring the Silver Fang back to reason?\u200b </div> </div> </div>It says right there at the start what the real issue is: jealousy. The guy clearly has some sort of inferiority complex. That's what you're dealing with. But of course, the book isn't saying that everybody in the Cult of Fenris has an inferiority-complex. And yet this case as described is thrown into the Hauglosk-bucket.<br /> <br /> What the game proposes is that similarly to just giving up via Harano, characters also have this doom-spiral towards losing their way in how to conduct their fighting. And yet it wasn't considered that this should be a character-issue rather than a doom-spiral you force on PCs. I would say that the mentioned Silver Fang didn't experience jealousy because Hauglosk forced him to feel that way but rather because it's a flaw of his personality. And yet, what W5 is proposing instead is that Hauglosk should be blamed for this happening.<br /> <br /> The mechanics are a whole other can of worms, of course...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T06:25:23-08:00","id":1531877,"title":"","content":"In all honesty, I'd do away with Hauglosk. Gheena from Sambrano's has more weight, but I generally would like there not being a &quot;Naughty&quot; mechanic.<br /> <br /> Also, because of the subject matter, I feel saying certain methods are bad is not going to go well. There is the soft way of trying to co-operate with people and then there is the rioting way of trying to get people to listen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T07:40:35-08:00","id":1531884,"title":"","content":"I think Hauglosk is something that a lot of players are struggling with because it's very badly defined more than it is a bad concept. Part of this is the question of what exactly is the warning signs, how many Garou are infected by it, and whether recognizing its existence is a recent thing or not.<br /> <br /> If this is really a recently diagnosed Garou condition then, yes, in fact a huge chunk of the Garou Nation not only may be infected but has been infected for millennia. How many Garou are infected? 1%? 2%? A third? What exactly qualfiies.<br /> <br /> In fact, i think part of the problem is they don't flat out make an obvious point in the game clear that would actually GIVE A DECENT CHRONICLE GOAL of saying, &quot;Yeah, a substantial chunk of the Garou Nation's leadership is corrupted by the Beast of War.&quot;<br /> <br /> (And yes, I'm going to think Hauglosk should be directly related to that even if you don't smell of the Wyrm)<br /> <br /> Make it clear to anyone LOOKING (and being strongly encouraged not to) that most of the Red Talons or at least their leadership are fully corrupted to Hauglosk. They just are smart enough to stick with the Garou nation for tactical reasons.<br /> <br /> It would explain a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T10:19:56-08:00","id":1531901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1531884#post1531884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make it clear to anyone LOOKING (and being strongly encouraged not to) that most of the Red Talons or at least their leadership are fully corrupted to Hauglosk. They just are smart enough to stick with the Garou nation for tactical reasons.<br /> <br /> It would explain a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the Talons, I feel a better alternative would be to offer other types of character examples than the ones we got. Because that is the biggest hangup with them in W5, if THEY can poison wells and eat people, what makes BSDs and CoF so much worse?<br /> <br /> Stuff like helping wolf-packs, ambassadors, junkyard dogs,etc. Make use of the fact that Talons are animal-focused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T10:38:03-08:00","id":1531903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1531901#post1531901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the Talons, I feel a better alternative would be to offer other types of character examples than the ones we got. Because that is the biggest hangup with them in W5, if THEY can poison wells and eat people, what makes BSDs and CoF so much worse?<br /> <br /> Stuff like helping wolf-packs, ambassadors, junkyard dogs,etc. Make use of the fact that Talons are animal-focused.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would require the writers not being directed to write Werewolf as if it were Vampire, I would guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T12:52:37-08:00","id":1531918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1531884#post1531884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Hauglosk is something that a lot of players are struggling with because it's very badly defined more than it is a bad concept. Part of this is the question of what exactly is the warning signs, how many Garou are infected by it, and whether recognizing its existence is a recent thing or not.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Make it clear to anyone LOOKING (and being strongly encouraged not to) that most of the Red Talons or at least their leadership are fully corrupted to Hauglosk. They just are smart enough to stick with the Garou nation for tactical reasons.<br /> <br /> It would explain a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realise that we only have what's in the book? And while you may want to build it into a better concept, as it stands it is not. It's literally a doom spiral that is applied based on OOC constraints rather in IC constraints and it ends with you being horrible. You should be able to be horrible without having a doctor's note to excuse it.<br /> <br /> And this uneven application is all over the Red Talons - the Red Talons are not presented as problematic. They are not presented as someone who is about to fall. They are not in any kind of special relationship with Hauglosk. They just do whatever they want and it's normalised by the book.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T13:12:05-08:00","id":1531921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1531918#post1531918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this uneven application is all over the Red Talons - the Red Talons are not presented as problematic. They are not presented as someone who is about to fall. They are not in any kind of special relationship with Hauglosk. They just do whatever they want and it's normalised by the book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly, the Red Talons are presented on equal level with other tribes.<br /> <br /> To showcase just how much this is making it a situation of 'rules for thee but not for me', here are two descriptions from W5 core. One is of a CoF antagonist. One is treated as a potential PC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W5 core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Plague Dog creeps into occupied territory, spreading terror and disease. Standing up and slugging it out with an enemy isn\u2019t their style; the Plague Dog prefers to mitigate risk to themselves and reduce their prey to quivering fear with a few snarls from the darkness, and \u2014 aided by a few choice pacts with disease spirits \u2014 a virulent bite that leaves the victims infected and contagious.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>W5 core</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> With a terrifying command of bellicose spirits, the Vindictive Theurge bolsters their packmates with brutal Gifts and causes enemies\u2019 wounds to feel as if they\u2019ve been sewn open with silver thread. With enough time to work their preferred rituals, they may even compel quiet on behalf of the spirits in the area, even silencing a pack\u2019s own caern guardian and preventing it from warning them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is worse, the theurge who uses spirits to hurt other garou, or the Talon who selfishly avoids conflict and instead spreads sickness?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T15:31:16-08:00","id":1531928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1531918#post1531918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realise that we only have what's in the book? And while you may want to build it into a better concept, as it stands it is not. It's literally a doom spiral that is applied based on OOC constraints rather in IC constraints and it ends with you being horrible. You should be able to be horrible without having a doctor's note to excuse it.<br /> <br /> And this uneven application is all over the Red Talons - the Red Talons are not presented as problematic. They are not presented as someone who is about to fall. They are not in any kind of special relationship with Hauglosk. They just do whatever they want and it's normalised by the book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be mixing a bunch of out of character and in character stuff.<br /> <br /> Hauglosk is in setting losing yourself to fanaticism and horrible zealotry. Which is something that Garou have been doing in-universe for millennia.<br /> <br /> They also do suffer from the Beast of War as canon since 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> It's not really a change other than it is showing that it can be subtle rather than overt like the frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-03T18:01:14-08:00","id":1531937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1531928#post1531928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That seems to be mixing a bunch of out of character and in character stuff.<br /> <br /> Hauglosk is in setting losing yourself to fanaticism and horrible zealotry. Which is something that Garou have been doing in-universe for millennia.<br /> <br /> <b>They also do suffer from the Beast of War as canon since 2nd Edition.</b><br /> <br /> It's not really a change other than it is showing that it can be subtle rather than overt like the frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the ill-fitting forced symmetry that maps Triatic Wyrms onto Breeds and made the game worse than just the possibility of eating your enemy in 1e? The forced angst mechanic that goes alongside Tribal Weaknesses per the apparent direction of &quot;well, it's in Vampire, so it should be in Werewolf...&quot;, where the &quot;it&quot; here is &quot;people being terrible&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T09:15:56-08:00","id":1531955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1531937#post1531937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean the ill-fitting forced symmetry that maps Triatic Wyrms onto Breeds and made the game worse than just the possibility of eating your enemy in 1e? The forced angst mechanic that goes alongside Tribal Weaknesses per the apparent direction of &quot;well, it's in Vampire, so it should be in Werewolf...&quot;, where the &quot;it&quot; here is &quot;people being terrible&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>The INCREDIBLY IMPORTANT element of the setting that the garou ARE infected by the Wyrm and yet assume they are immune?<br /> <br /> That is a major part of the setting. The Garou embrace their rage when they should be casting it aside. It is NOT a gift from Luna. It is an infection.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I don't know any book in the line that doesn't emphasize the Garou are partially corrupted and always teetering on the edge. That's their whole thing.<br /> <br /> They're warriors of gaia consumed with bloodlust that is self-destructive and always their own worst enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 03-04-2024, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T09:33:11-08:00","id":1531956,"title":"","content":"I can't help but note this discussion has become less about what changes we'd make and more about the specific changes W5 has made and why they're bad. While they are bad, there's a bunch of threads that exist already to criticize W5. That being said, I will note one thing:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1531955#post1531955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The INCREDIBLY IMPORTANT element of the setting that the garou ARE infected by the Wyrm and yet assume they are immune?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Garou have never assumed they're immune to being infected; the Black Spiral Dancers are a rather vivid reminder that they aren't and you have to buy a really costly merit to be immune to Wyrm emanations. In every book I've seen, the Garou are well aware that they're susceptible to Wyrm-taint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28383-citrakayah","name":"Citrakayah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28383_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T09:55:04-08:00","id":1531957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1531955#post1531955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The INCREDIBLY IMPORTANT element of the setting that the garou ARE infected by the Wyrm and yet assume they are immune?<br /> <br /> That is a major part of the setting. The Garou embrace their rage when they should be casting it aside. It is NOT a gift from Luna. It is an infection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why do Wyld-spirits have Rage? Why do books sometimes refer to Rage as the fury of Gaia out of character? And why is it that it wasn't Rage that caused all of the Garou's problems, but really shitty assumptions?<br /> <br /> Rage was never the problem. Overweening pride and arrogance, assuming one is so grand that only they're needed in the world - much as what one sees in humanity - was the problem. That set up the house of cards that saw the War of Rage, likely so-named either because most of the participants had it, it sounded grandiose, or because it was a convenient excuse. Possibly all three at once!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mind you, I don't know any book in the line that doesn't emphasize the Garou are partially corrupted and always teetering on the edge. That's their whole thing.<br /> <br /> They're warriors of gaia consumed with bloodlust that is self-destructive and always their own worst enemy. </div> </div> </div>That's not actually in the books, and Rage wasn't supposed to be DSotBH-style Vicissitude. In fact, Thrall of the Wyrm didn't show up until 2e, and some Fera don't have it at all in spite of having Rage. Meanwhile, a lot of Hatar become corrupt and horribly, shitty people without having it. Must be the Blood Pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T11:30:52-08:00","id":1531961,"title":"","content":"I think that Hauglosk works perfectly well as the opposite of Harano if you assume that they are, at bottom, just different faces of the same problem - a sort of Supernatural PTSD that afflicts the Garou because each of them is, in many ways, a Fighting Spirit clothed in flesh and the sheer weight of the Apocalypse War (Pressing down on a steadily dwindling and never especially large number of warriors) can do a serious number on even the strongest spirit of one does not properly manage the grief, rage and soul-deep weariness that goes with being a Spirit Warrior Werewolf.<br /> <br /> The key thing to remember is that the best way for a Garou to manage all this is to work and fight as part of a wider community, to honour the customs of their forebears and be honoured by their peers, to practice the proper rituals and remember that there IS a point to their ongoing, one-sided struggle against the Forces of Stasis &amp; Entropy (Even if it\u2019s only that they keep the world turning and their Kin free from the Wyrm for one more day).<br /> <br /> Above all, it\u2019s crucial that a Garou walk the middle way between despair and desperate rage (\u2018Balance in All Things\u2019 really ought to be one of THE Garou mantras).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-04T12:27:39-08:00","id":1531972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th#post1530740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ICONS OF RAGE is awesome and OPP is the last gasp of the heavy continuity of the previous editions that we all fell in love with. So, the question would be how would you update the setting to the year 2024?<br /> <br /> Assuming that Gaia isn't dead or dying and the Cult of Fenris didn't exist.<br /> <br /> Feel free to suggest big changes but we're using W20 as a basis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really paint a complete picture for a developed W20 setting, but I could tell a bit how I advanced the setting for my own chronicles since Revised. Naturally, that is biased around the PCs and their actions, and running cross-splat chronicles also factors into it.<br /> <br /> Gaia isn't dead but on life support. Comatose or delirious at best. It's bad. That reverberates down through the ranks of gaian spirits, who have become more erratic and detached from the Garou. It's also sinking in that the impact of the Weaver as enabler for the Wyrm has been severely underestimated.<br /> <br /> The Garou Nation still exists but is in the process of dissolving. This began in the Industrial Age and then accelerated considerably with the Information Age. A political and philosophical divide has started to grow between two factions of the tribes: adapt to the new situation or double down on the old ways, with the Glass Walkers being a strong proponent of the former and the Talons of the latter. You can tell that this also results in an increasing dissonance between breeds; the contrast between growing up wolf-born or human-born is so stark that both sides have difficulty relating to each other. Garou-born are, as always, caught in the middle.<br /> <br /> Further complicating this is a generational disconnect, in which antiquated customs and laws clash horribly with modern sensibilities. While that isn't anything new, up until the 1980s these problems were mostly stifled by the lack of a global communication network that allows the youngsters to talk with each other and organize - which they do now. There are inter-tribe 'anarchist' cells forming which eschew tradition and who think they can help Gaia better outside of the rules of the rigid framework of the Nation. Some are idealistic radicals, some are moderates, and they have wildly different ideas. They however share the believe that the ways of their ancestors did not really accomplish anything and that time is running out. Some elders would describe those cells as terrorists within the Nation.<br /> <br /> The Stargazers leaving and the appearance of the Ahadi were powerful catalysts for many (especially those young idealists) to finally try and smooth things out between the Garou and the other Fera, because the Garou are also losing the numbers game. Wolf populations going up in some places is great, but compared to, say, 300 years ago it's hardly anything. Now contrast this to the populations of rats and spiders. The other Fera, on their end, are extremely skeptical of any would-be defectors from the Nation. They have been burnt too often, but on the other hand aren't blind to the fact that time is running out.<br /> <br /> There are also careful overtures towards similarly disillusioned parties of mortals and other splats. The idea that outsiders might too think the death of Gaia is bad and maybe <i>help</i> is losing its taboo. Mages and Sorcerers mostly, but at least in my games the Mummies also have a close eye on the situation. Vampires are still considered bad mojo, though. For what it's worth, the Umbra is still accessible and has become a focus to look for alternative solutions.<br /> <br /> The tldr is that the Nation is standing on its own feet while trying to rush into different directions, panicked by the escalating situation. My players need to juggle navigating a failing system while finding and pushing their own solutions outside of it, at least until the disparate alliances of the 'anarchists' are strong enough to stand on their own. If saving Gaia is too big a goal for a single pack, enacting the changes that need to happen to make that even possible is far more attainable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:40:17-08:00","id":1532015,"title":"","content":"In all honesty this sounds like an intriguing, if rather<br /> melancholy take on things.<br /> <br /> On a more cheerful note, I\u2019ve been toying with ideas on the Best way to make the WW20 setting and the W5th version of things stand out from each other; for some reason the key notion that occurs to me is that the WW20 World of Darkness circa AD 2024 looks very like a 1990s cinematic vision of the \u2018Near Future\u2019 rather than the 2020s we\u2019ve come to know and grudgingly tolerate \u2026<br /> <br /> (In terms of production design, that is).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T06:53:53-08:00","id":1532021,"title":"","content":"In all honesty, I think porting Hauglosk makes little sense. For one, if we use the old Rage (which we SHOULD), that is already a punishment mechanic for extremism. The more Rage you have the harder it is to be a person and not a killing machine.<br /> <br /> Unlike W5 Rage which has none of the appeal, Legacy Rage is already a perfect trap. The more you have the better you are at combat and using gifts. But you lose who you are to the Rage.<br /> <br /> On top of this, this kind of mechanic MIGHT work if the PCs were humans turned into garou. Something against their very nature that they now have to justify to themselves (like vampires have humanity and paths.)<br /> <br /> And finally, WtA Legacy is about protecting Gaia and existence itself. Not just humanity and the current crop of animals on earth. What is extreme in one situation might not be enough in another. A finger waggling mechanic isn't really suitable when there is no right answer to some issues garou face.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T07:14:14-08:00","id":1532024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1532021#post1532021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all honesty, I think porting Hauglosk makes little sense. For one, if we use the old Rage (which we SHOULD), that is already a punishment mechanic for extremism. The more Rage you have the harder it is to be a person and not a killing machine.<br /> <br /> Unlike W5 Rage which has none of the appeal, Legacy Rage is already a perfect trap. The more you have the better you are at combat and using gifts. But you lose who you are to the Rage.<br /> <br /> On top of this, this kind of mechanic MIGHT work if the PCs were humans turned into garou. Something against their very nature that they now have to justify to themselves (like vampires have humanity and paths.)<br /> <br /> And finally, WtA Legacy is about protecting Gaia and existence itself. Not just humanity and the current crop of animals on earth. What is extreme in one situation might not be enough in another. A finger waggling mechanic isn't really suitable when there is no right answer to some issues garou face.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if anything whatever changes one brings to W5 needs to pursue the goal of going even harder for the negativity, hopelessness and despair of the Age of Apocalypse setting. Because in W5 Rage isn't just a punishment for having too much of it. Since Gnosis was removed, Rage was also turned into a sort-of battery for certain Gifts and Rites. But then you also have &quot;Losing the wolf&quot;. W5 doesn't just punish PCs for having too much Rage but also punishes them for having too little (or none). So the mechanics aren't even pushing for a message of &quot;Rage is bad, you should avoid it.&quot;, they're pushing more towards a &quot;pick your poison&quot;-situation. It's just all downsides no matter how much or how little Rage a PC has.<br /> <br /> And so, really, I think, the only way to bring the narrative level on the same level as these mechanics would be to go for a far darker setting that embraces the negative portrayal of the Garou and the dire state of things in the W5 setting. On the other hand, trying to make W20 sentiments work within that system would take <i>a lot</i> of changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-05T08:16:38-08:00","id":1532032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1530740-hypothetical-if-we-were-to-update-wta-to-5th-edition-using-20th?p=1532015#post1532015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all honesty this sounds like an intriguing, if rather melancholy take on things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess that is the legacy of me having started WoD with Vampire. In the long term I see some guy named Martin nail 95 Theses Why The Nation Sucks to a caern and cause a schism that results in splitting the Nation into one half that resembles the Ahadi and another that has all the traditionalists. After the inevitable bad blood period and lots of fur flying I can even see the two get along on a 'professional' basis, which would probably the best case scenario.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T14:25:17-08:00","id":1532114,"title":"","content":"I believe that the By Night studios version of WEREWOLF has almost exactly that idea as one of it\u2019s core elements: you might like to check it out, if possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}